From b21df41a584383c0425965fa4c6fd528165a92d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:18:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/19] ggml-backend: memoize backend-support verdicts in sched
 assignment (A5-C3, W6-9 gradino C3)

split_graph() re-derives the same supports_op()/supports_buft() verdicts on
every eval for graphs that repeat with stable topology (decode MTP: ~7.7
evals/round, same weight buffers, same shapes per token count). Route the six
scheduler-side query sites through two memos:

- supports_op: signature-keyed, 2-way set-associative. The signature captures
  every tensor field read by the in-tree supports_op implementations
  (ggml-vulkan, ggml-cpu, amx/repack/kleidiai/spacemit extras): op, type, ne,
  nb, flags, op_params word 0 for UNARY/GLU/UPSCALE (vk reads the interpolate
  mode/antialias bits of UPSCALE at ggml-vulkan.cpp:17729-17733; the multimodal
  mtmd path sets those dynamically) plus SCALE as a defensive superset, and
  words 0..3 for SOFT_MAX_BACK (cpu max_bias). Any field change = signature
  mismatch = full recompute; ops with >3 srcs bypass the memo. Exact memcmp
  validation on every hit (the stored hash is only a pre-filter).
- supports_buft: keyed on (buft, backend), both immutable for the scheduler
  lifetime.

The memos survive sched resets by design (cross-eval reuse), never change the
assignment algorithm, and degrade to direct calls when disabled
(GGML_SCHED_ASSIGN_MEMO=0, default on) or when allocation fails. Memo stats
(queries/hits) logged at sched_free with GGML_SCHED_DEBUG=1.

Gate N (bit-exact): harness with 1- and 2-backend scheds over 3 rounds of 17
representative evals (recurrences, token-count variants, verify/drafter-like
alternation, same weight consumed by different ops, SILU/GELU params variants,
UPSCALE with BILINEAR|ANTIALIAS / NEAREST / BICUBIC op_params variants, FA with
4 srcs = bypass, view_src on pre-allocated cache, forced backend-1 island):
node-assignment and output digests identical memo ON vs OFF (main passes:
so-memo hits 318/378 and 327/396). Dedicated UPSCALE sub-sched proves the
variants produce distinct signatures: 6 queries / 3 misses with the fix vs
6 queries / 1 miss on a control build without it. test-backend-ops output
identical ON vs OFF.
Logs: logs/wave6/w6c3/, report: docs/research/wave6/w6c3-report.md

Review fix (spec review on 3d1089a4b): UPSCALE was missing from the params
whitelist - a false hit could assign VK without the antialias pipeline.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai
